Subject: winemac: drop the foreground when the app is deactivated

macdrv_app_deactivated() gave up the foreground window only when

    get_active_window() == NtUserGetForegroundWindow()

held.  get_active_window() is GUITHREADINFO for GetCurrentThreadId() -- the
active window of whichever thread pumped the event -- while the foreground
window is global, and APP_DEACTIVATED is process-wide and names no window, so
the two coincided only by luck.  When they did not, the foreground stayed put,
win32u saw no change of foreground thread, and no WM_ACTIVATEAPP was ever
delivered: the program was never told the user had switched away.

winex11 has no such gap.  The X FocusOut event names the window that lost
focus, so focus_out() compares that window rather than substituting a
per-thread lookup.

Check what actually matters instead: that the foreground window is ours.

Found with Super Street Fighter IV, where the missing WM_ACTIVATEAPP left the
game believing it still had focus -- its DirectInput pad stayed unacquired
because it never re-Acquired, and it kept submitting frames to a window the
compositor had stopped displaying until the Metal drawable pool ran out and
dxvk-submit blocked in nextDrawable.

Covered by tests/app-activation-test.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1813,9 +1813,16 @@
  */
 void macdrv_app_deactivated(void)
 {
+    HWND foreground = NtUserGetForegroundWindow();
+    DWORD procid = 0;
+
     NtUserClipCursor(NULL);
 
-    if (get_active_window() == NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
+    /* APP_DEACTIVATED is process-wide and names no window; get_active_window()
+     * is per-thread, so comparing it against the global foreground window
+     * matched only when this thread happened to own the foreground. */
+    if (foreground && NtUserGetWindowThread(foreground, &procid) &&
+        procid == GetCurrentProcessId())
     {
         TRACE("setting fg to desktop\n");
         NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
